{
  "message": {
    "toRecipients": [
      {
        "emailAddress": {
          "address": "ossgenai.im@pg.com"
        }
      }
    ],
    "ccRecipients": [],
    "bccRecipients": []
  },
  "comment": "FOR ROUTING USE WORKFLOW=na_om_data_agent (AskOM)<br><br>\n<strong>IMPORTANT - SAME THREAD READ SCOPE:</strong> This is a direct reply inside the existing Outlook conversation, not a forward. Use the latest actual customer email available in the reply history below this prompt. Do not use the subject alone. Ignore system-generated status/error emails, process completion emails, signatures, disclaimers, and older unrelated replies.<br><br>\n<strong>Mandatory validation before extracting:</strong><br>\nOnly continue if the actual customer email contains BOTH:<br>\n1) a real request to ride-with, ship-with, consolidate, attach/load with another PO, or make one PO ride with another PO; and<br>\n2) at least one explicit PO number tied to PO context such as PO, PO#, PO #, purchase order, order, main PO, rider PO, or a PO table/list.<br><br>\nIf the email is a system/status/error notification, or if either requirement is missing, respond exactly: Is not a consolidation<br><br>\nIf it passes validation, extract the consolidation details from the original customer email in this same conversation.<br><br>\nReturn a table with exactly 2 columns: Truck # and PO #<br>\nEach row must contain exactly one PO only. Never place multiple PO numbers in the same PO # cell. If multiple POs belong to the same truck, create one separate row per PO and repeat the same Truck # value on each row.<br>\nRemove all internal spaces from every PO number (e.g. \"07 291073\" → \"07291073\"). Output PO numbers as a single unbroken string with no spaces.<br>\nUse Truck #1 as standard. If the customer sends more than one consolidation, use Truck #2, Truck #3, etc.<br>\n@{replace(variables('SignatureHtml'),'"','\"')}\n<p style=\"font-size:1px;color:#ffffff;line-height:1px\">AWG-FLOW-ID: @{outputs('Compose_Correlation_FlowId')} | AWG-STEP: CONSOLIDATION_CONFIRM</p>"
}
